menu "My UPS Pal login"

config UPSA_DEFAULT_ADMIN_USER
    string "Default admin username (empty: no default login)"
    default ""
    help
        Seeded into NVS by auth_init() on a board that has no login stored,
        so the board is usable the moment it powers up and the setup page does
        not have to insist on a login before it will do anything.

        EMPTY IS THE UPSTREAM BEHAVIOUR and the default: no login exists until
        someone chooses one, and the setup form requires it. Leave it empty
        unless a deployment has a reason to ship a known login.

        A default set here is compiled into the image, and under GPL the
        corresponding source goes to whoever receives that image -- so treat
        anything set here as public. A per-device default derived from the MAC
        is stronger if you can label the boards.

config UPSA_DEFAULT_ADMIN_PASS
    string "Default admin password"
    default ""
    help
        Used only when UPSA_DEFAULT_ADMIN_USER is set. 8-64 characters, no
        spaces or quotes (authc_shape_ok). Stored salted and hashed like any
        other password; only this build-time string is plain text.

        While the login is still this default, auth_is_default() is true and
        the web page says so. It is a notice, not a gate: nothing is blocked.

endmenu
